meta {
  name: List purchases
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchases
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 10
  ~sort: id
  ~order: desc
  ~search: a
  ~userId: 1
  ~paymentStatus: PENDING
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # List purchases

  Orders with their product lines. Totals are computed by the server from each product's current price and are never accepted from the client: each line's `amount` is `price × quantity`, `totalAmount` is the sum of the lines, and `finalAmount` is `totalAmount + taxes − discountAmount`, floored at 0. Quantities and unit prices are kept in `data.lines`. After creation only `reference`, `paymentStatus`, `invoice`, `paymentDate` and `data` can change.

  Returns one page of active purchases. Soft-deleted records never appear.

  ## Auth

  Bearer token of a user whose role is `ADMIN` (send **auth/Log in** first; it stores `{{token}}`).

  ## Query parameters

  | Name | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `page` | integer | no | 1-based page; default 1. A page past the end returns `data: []` with correct `pagination`. |
  | `limit` | integer | no | Page size; default 10; values above 100 are clamped to 100. |
  | `sort` | string | no | One of: id, createdAt, finalAmount, paymentDate. Default `id`. |
  | `order` | string | no | `asc` or `desc`; default `desc`. |
  | `search` | string | no | Case-insensitive match against: reference, invoice. |
  | `userId` | integer | no | Only this user's purchases. |
  | `paymentStatus` | string | no | One of `PENDING`, `SUCCESS`, `FAILED`, `REJECTED`. |

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK

    {
      "message": "Purchase list",
      "data": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "userId": 1,
          "reference": "WEB-1001",
          "totalAmount": "29.9",
          "taxes": "2.99",
          "discountAmount": "0",
          "finalAmount": "32.89",
          "paymentStatus": "PENDING",
          "invoice": null,
          "paymentDate": null,
          "data": {
            "lines": [
              {
                "productId": 1,
                "quantity": 2,
                "unitPrice": "14.95"
              }
            ]
          },
          "user": {
            "id": 1,
            "name": "Store",
            "lastName": "Administrator",
            "email": "admin@lpaecomms.test"
          },
          "products": [
            {
              "id": 1,
              "purchaseId": 1,
              "productId": 1,
              "amount": "29.9",
              "product": {
                "id": 1,
                "name": "Wireless Headphones",
                "code": "wireless-headphones"
              }
            }
          ],
          "created": {
            "client": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
            "server": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
            "serverDate": "2026-09-27",
            "serverTime": "12:30:14",
            "unixTime": 1790476214,
            "user": 1,
            "role": "ADMIN"
          },
          "updated": null,
          "statusName": "ACTIVE",
          "status": 1,
          "createdAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z"
        }
      ],
      "pagination": {
        "total": 1,
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 10,
        "totalPages": 1,
        "count": 1,
        "hasNextPage": false,
        "hasPrevPage": false
      }
    }

  ### 400 Bad Request — validation failed

  A paging, sort or filter parameter is invalid (e.g. `page=0`, an unknown `sort`).

    {
      "message": "Some fields need attention.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "page",
          "message": "Invalid input"
        }
      ]
    }

  ### 401 Unauthorized — missing, invalid or expired token

    {
      "message": "Sign in to continue.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 403 Forbidden — the token's role is not ADMIN

    {
      "message": "You do not have permission to do this.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  Outside production, error bodies also carry `stack`.
}
